WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Speaker 1: So almost immediately after Nikki&nbsp;
Haley's announcement that she's running for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:10.200
president through the Republican nomination in&nbsp;
2024, the Trump campaign put out a confusing and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.000
bizarre campaign email attacking Nikki Haley.&nbsp;
And what's really fascinating about this email,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.880
which we'll look at in a moment, is it attacked&nbsp;
Nikki Haley for being too much of a leftist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:28.080
but also for being too extreme on the right. It&nbsp;
is as confusing and bizarre as everything we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:35.400
come to expect and see from the Trump campaign.&nbsp;
Take a look at this. So the first lines are first.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.300
It's called the real Nikki Haley. First of all,&nbsp;
Trump's going to tell you who the real Nikki Haley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.240
is. Okay. It starts by saying Hillary Clinton is&nbsp;
an inspiration to Nikki Haley. In a 2012 interview&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:49.860
with The New York Times, Nikki Haley said, The&nbsp;
reason I actually ran for office is because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:55.920
Hillary Clinton. So here it wants to tag Nikki&nbsp;
Haley. It wants to trash Nikki Haley by saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:02.400
she's really not a conservative because she&nbsp;
was inspired by Hillary Clinton. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:07.200
it ignores the uncontroversial reality that&nbsp;
you could disagree with Hillary Clinton's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:15.300
politics. But see Hillary Clinton's success as an&nbsp;
elected official and public servant, as someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:20.940
who is a woman as inspirational. That's not super&nbsp;
controversial, but she's not really on the right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:25.200
She's on the left because she was inspired&nbsp;
by Hillary. And then in the next sentence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:31.620
Trump slams Nikki Haley for supporting&nbsp;
Paul Ryan's plan for entitlement reform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:39.240
which threatened Medicare and Social Security,&nbsp;
saying, quote, Haley praised Ryan's Medicare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:47.340
proposal at the time and said lawmakers should&nbsp;
examine Medicare and Social Security spending to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:53.880
address federal debt. Then quoting Nikki Haley&nbsp;
herself from 2010, saying what they need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:00.120
doing is looking at entitlements. Look at Social&nbsp;
Security, Look at Medicaid. Look at Medicare. Look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.820
at these things. Let's go to the heart of what&nbsp;
is causing government to grow and tackle that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:12.480
They're playing that. Nikki Haley is too extreme&nbsp;
in what she wants to cut and in the government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:19.980
spending she wants to reduce, which is normally&nbsp;
an attack that the left makes on the right. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:28.140
Haley's a leftist and Haley is too far right.&nbsp;
It's not coherent. But in the defense of Trump,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:36.240
Haley's campaign isn't very coherent so far. And&nbsp;
Trump's attacks on her are also not coherent. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:43.140
Nikki Haley at some point might want to articulate&nbsp;
what policy is she actually running on. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.300
I say she might want to articulate it because as&nbsp;
I said earlier in the program, it's not clear that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:56.700
she needs any policy in order to win a Republican&nbsp;
primary. Trump had some policy statements in 2016.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.560
Most of them we all knew were never going to be&nbsp;
achieved. He wasn't going to replace Obamacare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.460
and he wasn't going to build a wall that Mexico&nbsp;
was going to pay for, and he wasn't going to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:09.600
all the things he claimed. It didn't really&nbsp;
matter. It's not clear that these Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.940
care about policy enough to hold it against Nikki&nbsp;
Haley, but at a certain point, she'll have to come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.600
up with something that at least she can put on&nbsp;
her website. And that hasn't happened yet. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:25.020
all incoherent. And this is exactly what I would&nbsp;
expect much more of in this Republican primary.

